H3600.strongs:
Origin: a form for 3564 (only in the dual);
Meaning: a cooking range (consisting of two parallel stones, across which the boiler is set)
KJV renders: ranges for pots.

H3602.strongs:
Origin: from 3541;
Meaning: just so, referring to the previous or following context
KJV renders: after that (this) manner, this matter, (even) so, in such a case, thus.

H3603.strongs:
Origin: from 3769;
Meaning: a circle, i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf; also a talent (or large [round] coin)
KJV renders: loaf, morsel, piece, plain, talent.

H3604.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3603;
Meaning: a talent
KJV renders: talent.

H3605.strongs:
Origin: or (Jeremiah 33:8) כּוֹל; from 3634;
Meaning: properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)
KJV renders: (in) all (manner, (ye)), altogether, any (manner), enough, every (one, place, thing), howsoever, as many as, (no-) thing, ought, whatsoever, (the) whole, whoso(-ever).

H3607.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to restrict, by act (hold back or in) or word (prohibit)
KJV renders: finish, forbid, keep (back), refrain, restrain, retain, shut up, be stayed, withhold.

H3608.strongs:
Origin: from 3607;
Meaning: a prison
KJV renders: prison. Compare 3610, 3628.

H3609.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 3607 and 1; restraint of (his) father;
Meaning: Kilab, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chileab.

H3610.strongs:
Origin: dual of 3608 in the original sense of separation;
Meaning: two heterogeneities
KJV renders: divers seeds (-e kinds), mingled (seed).

H3611.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root means. to yelp, or else to attack;
Meaning: a dog; hence (by euphemism) a male prostitute
KJV renders: dog.

H3612.strongs:
Origin: perhaps a form of 3611, or else from the same root in the sense of forcible;
Meaning: Caleb, the name of three Israelites
KJV renders: Caleb.

H3613.strongs:
Origin: from 3612 and 672;
Meaning: Caleb-Ephrathah, a place in Egypt (if the text is correct)
KJV renders: Caleb-ephrathah.

H3614.strongs:
Origin: probably by erroneous transcription for כָּלֵבִי; patronymically from 3612;
Meaning: a Calebite or descendant of Caleb
KJV renders: of the house of Caleb.

H3615.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to end, whether intransitive (to cease, be finished, perish) or transitive (to complete, prepare, consume)
KJV renders: accomplish, cease, consume (away), determine, destroy (utterly), be (when... were) done, (be an) end (of), expire, (cause to) fail, faint, finish, fulfil, × fully, × have, leave (off), long, bring to pass, wholly reap, make clean riddance, spend, quite take away, waste.

H3616.strongs:
Origin: from 3615;
Meaning: pining
KJV renders: fail.

H3617.strongs:
Origin: from 3615;
Meaning: a completion; adverb, completely; also destruction
KJV renders: altogether, (be, utterly) consume(-d), consummation(-ption), was determined, (full, utter) end, riddance.

H3618.strongs:
Origin: from 3634;
Meaning: a bride (as if perfect); hence, a son's wife
KJV renders: bride, daughter-in-law, spouse.

H3619.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 3611;
Meaning: a bird-trap (as furnished with a clap-stick or treadle to spring it); hence, a basket (as resembling a wicker cage)
KJV renders: basket, cage.

H3620.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3619;
Meaning: Kelub, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Chelub.

H3621.strongs:
Origin: a form of 3612;
Meaning: Kelubai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chelubai.

H3622.strongs:
Origin: from 3615; completed;
Meaning: Keluhai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chelluh.

H3623.strongs:
Origin: denominative passive participle from 3618;
Meaning: bridehood (only in the plural)
KJV renders: espousal.

H3624.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to be complete;
Meaning: maturity
KJV renders: full (old) age.

H3625.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3624;
Meaning: Kelach, a place in Assyria
KJV renders: Calah.

H3626.strongs:
Origin: from 3605 and 2374; every seer;
Meaning: Col-Chozeh, an Israelite
KJV renders: Col-hozeh.

H3627.strongs:
Origin: from 3615;
Meaning: something prepared, i.e. any apparatus (as an implement, utensil, dress, vessel or weapon)
KJV renders: armour(-bearer), artillery, bag, carriage, furnish, furniture, instrument, jewel, that is made of, × one from another, that which pertaineth, pot, psaltery, sack, stuff, thing, tool, vessel, ware, weapon, whatsoever.

H3628.strongs:
Origin: or כְּלוּא; from 3627 (compare 3608);
Meaning: a prison
KJV renders: prison.

H3629.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3627 (only in the plural);
Meaning: a kidney (as an essential organ); figuratively, the mind (as the interior self)
KJV renders: kidneys, reins.

H3630.strongs:
Origin: a form of 3631;
Meaning: Kiljon, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chilion.

H3631.strongs:
Origin: from 3615;
Meaning: pining, destruction
KJV renders: consumption, failing.

H3632.strongs:
Origin: from 3634;
Meaning: complete; as noun, the whole (specifically, a sacrifice entirely consumed); as adverb, fully
KJV renders: all, every whit, flame, perfect(-ion), utterly, whole burnt offering (sacrifice), wholly.

H3633.strongs:
Origin: from 3557; sustenance;
Meaning: Calcol, an Israelite
KJV renders: Calcol, Chalcol.

H3634.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to complete
KJV renders: (make) perfect.

H3635.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3634;
Meaning: to complete
KJV renders: finish, make (set) up.

H3636.strongs:
Origin: from 3634; complete;
Meaning: Kelal, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chelal.

H3637.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to wound; but only figuratively, to taunt or insult
KJV renders: be (make) ashamed, blush, be confounded, be put to confusion, hurt, reproach, (do, put to) shame.

H3638.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Kilmad, a place apparently in the Assyrian empire
KJV renders: Chilmad.

H3639.strongs:
Origin: from 3637;
Meaning: disgrace
KJV renders: confusion, dishonour, reproach, shame.

H3640.strongs:
Origin: from 3639;
Meaning: disgrace
KJV renders: shame.

H3641.strongs:
Origin: or כַּלְנֵה; also כַּלְנוֹ; of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Calneh or Calno, a place in the Assyrian empire
KJV renders: Calneh, Calno. Compare 3656.

H3642.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to pine after
KJV renders: long.

H3643.strongs:
Origin: from 3642; pining;
Meaning: Kimham, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chimham.

H3644.strongs:
Origin: or כָּמוֹ; a form of the prefix k, but used separately [compare 3651];
Meaning: as, thus, so
KJV renders: according to, (such) as (it were, well as), in comparison of, like (as, to, unto), thus, when, worth.

H3645.strongs:
Origin: or (Jeremiah 48:7) כְּמִישׁ; from an unused root meaning to subdue; the powerful;
Meaning: Kemosh, the god of the Moabites
KJV renders: Chemosh.

H3646.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to store up or preserve;
Meaning: 'cummin' (from its use as a condiment)
KJV renders: cummin.

H3647.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to store away, i.e. (figuratively) in the memory
KJV renders: lay up in store.

H3648.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to intertwine or contract, i.e. (by implication) to shrivel (as with heat); figuratively, to be deeply affected with passion (love or pity)
KJV renders: be black, be kindled, yearn.

H3649.strongs:
Origin: from 3648;
Meaning: properly, an ascetic (as if shrunk with self-maceration), i.e. an idolatrous priest (only in plural)
KJV renders: Chemarims (idolatrous) priests.

H3650.strongs:
Origin: redupl. from 3648;
Meaning: obscuration (as if from shrinkage of light), i.e. an eclipse (only in plural)
KJV renders: blackness.

H3651.strongs:
Origin: from 3559;
Meaning: properly, set upright; hence (figuratively as adjective) just; but usually (as adverb or conjunction) rightly or so (in various applications to manner, time and relation; often with other particles)
KJV renders: after that (this, -ward, -wards), as... as, (for-) asmuch as yet, be (for which) cause, following, howbeit, in (the) like (manner, -wise), × the more, right, (even) so, state, straightway, such (thing), surely, there (where) -fore, this, thus, true, well, × you.

H3652.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3651;
Meaning: so
KJV renders: thus.

H3653.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3651, used as a noun;
Meaning: a stand, i.e. pedestal or station
KJV renders: base, estate, foot, office, place, well.

H3655.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to address by an additional name; hence, to eulogize
KJV renders: give flattering titles, surname (himself).

H3656.strongs:
Origin: for 3641;
Meaning: Canneh, a place in Assyria
KJV renders: Canneh.

H3657.strongs:
Origin: from 3661;
Meaning: a plant (as set)
KJV renders: × vineyard.

H3658.strongs:
Origin: from a unused root meaning to twang;
Meaning: a harp
KJV renders: harp.

H3659.strongs:
Origin: for 3204;
Meaning: Conjah, an Israelite king
KJV renders: Coniah.

H3660.strongs:
