Meaning: Kenanjah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chenaniah.

H3664.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to collect; hence, to enfold
KJV renders: gather (together), heap up, wrap self.

H3665.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to bend the knee; hence, to humiliate, vanquish
KJV renders: bring down (low), into subjection, under, humble (self), subdue.

H3666.strongs:
Origin: from 3665 in the sense of folding (compare 3664);
Meaning: a package
KJV renders: wares.

H3667.strongs:
Origin: from 3665; humiliated;
Meaning: Kenaan, a son a Ham; also the country inhabited by him
KJV renders: Canaan, merchant, traffick.

H3668.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3667;
Meaning: Kenaanah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Chenaanah.

H3669.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 3667;
Meaning: a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans)
KJV renders: Canaanite, merchant, trafficker.

H3670.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to project laterally, i.e. probably (reflexive) to withdraw
KJV renders: be removed.

H3671.strongs:
Origin: from 3670;
Meaning: an edge or extremity; specifically (of a bird or army) a wing, (of a garment or bedclothing) a flap, (of the earth) a quarter, (of a building) a pinnacle
KJV renders: bird, border, corner, end, feather(-ed), × flying, (one an-) other, overspreading, × quarters, skirt, × sort, uttermost part, wing(-ed).

H3672.strongs:
Origin: or כִּנֶּרֶתlemma כִּנֶרֶת missing dagesh, corrected to כִּנֶּרֶת; respectively plural and singular feminine from the same as 3658; perhaps harp-shaped;
Meaning: Kinneroth or Kinnereth, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chinnereth, Chinneroth, Cinneroth.

H3673.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3664;
Meaning: to assemble
KJV renders: gather together.

H3674.strongs:
Origin: from 3655;
Meaning: a colleague (as having the same title)
KJV renders: companion.

H3677.strongs:
Origin: or כֶּסֶה; apparently from 3680;
Meaning: properly, fulness or the full moon, i.e. its festival
KJV renders: (time) appointed.

H3678.strongs:
Origin: or כִּסֵּה; from 3680;
Meaning: properly, covered, i.e. a throne (as canopied)
KJV renders: seat, stool, throne.

H3680.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to plump, i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy)
KJV renders: clad self, close, clothe, conceal, cover (self), (flee to) hide, overwhelm. Compare 3780.

H3681.strongs:
Origin: passive participle of 3680;
Meaning: properly, covered, i.e. (as noun) a covering
KJV renders: covering.

H3682.strongs:
Origin: from 3680;
Meaning: a cover (garment); figuratively, a veiling
KJV renders: covering, raiment, vesture.

H3683.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to cut off
KJV renders: cut down (up).

H3684.strongs:
Origin: from 3688;
Meaning: properly, fat, i.e. (figuratively) stupid or silly
KJV renders: fool(-ish).

H3685.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3684;
Meaning: any notable constellation; specifically Orion (as if a burly one)
KJV renders: constellation, Orion.

H3686.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3684;
Meaning: Kesil, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chesil.

H3687.strongs:
Origin: from 3684;
Meaning: silliness
KJV renders: foolish.

H3688.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to be fat, i.e. (figuratively) silly
KJV renders: be foolish.

H3689.strongs:
Origin: from 3688;
Meaning: properly, fatness, i.e. by implication (literally) the loin (as the seat of the leaf fat) or (generally) the viscera; also (figuratively) silliness or (in a good sense) trust
KJV renders: confidence, flank, folly, hope, loin.

H3690.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3689;
