KJV renders: Chisleu.

H3692.strongs:
Origin: from 3688; hopeful;
Meaning: Kislon, an Israelite
KJV renders: Chislon.

H3693.strongs:
Origin: from 3688; fertile;
Meaning: Kesalon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chesalon.

H3694.strongs:
Origin: feminine plural of passive participle of 3688; fattened;
Meaning: Kesulloth, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chesulloth.

H3695.strongs:
Origin: a plural probably of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Casluchim, a people cognate to the Egyptians
KJV renders: Casluhim.

H3696.strongs:
Origin: from the feminine plural of 3689 and 8396; flanks of Tabor;
Meaning: Kisloth-Tabor, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chisloth-tabor.

H3697.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to shear
KJV renders: × only, poll. Compare 3765.

H3698.strongs:
Origin: from 3697;
Meaning: spelt (from its bristliness as if just shorn)
KJV renders: fitches, rie.

H3699.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to estimate
KJV renders: make count.

H3700.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to become pale, i.e. (by implication) to pine after; also to fear
KJV renders: (have) desire, be greedy, long, sore.

H3701.strongs:
Origin: from 3700;
Meaning: silver (from its pale color); by implication, money
KJV renders: money, price, silver(-ling).

H3703.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from 3701; silvery;
Meaning: Casiphja, a place in Babylon
KJV renders: Casiphia.

H3704.strongs:
Origin: from 3680;
Meaning: a cushion or pillow (as covering a seat or bed)
KJV renders: pillow.

H3705.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) probably from 3652;
Meaning: now
KJV renders: now.

H3706.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or כְּעֶת; (Aramaic), feminine of 3705;
Meaning: thus (only in the formula 'and so forth')
KJV renders: at such a time.

H3707.strongs:
