H3708.strongs:
Origin: or (in Job) כַּעַשׂ; from 3707;
Meaning: vexation
KJV renders: anger, angry, grief, indignation, provocation, provoking, × sore, sorrow, spite, wrath.

H3709.strongs:
Origin: from 3721;
Meaning: the hollow hand or palm (so of the paw of an animal, of the sole, and even of the bowl of a dish or sling, the handle of a bolt, the leaves of a palm-tree); figuratively, power
KJV renders: branch, foot, hand((-ful), -dle, (-led)), hollow, middle, palm, paw, power, sole, spoon.

H3710.strongs:
Origin: from 3721;
Meaning: a hollow rock
KJV renders: rock.

H3711.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to bend, i.e. (figuratively) to tame or subdue
KJV renders: pacify.

H3712.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3709;
Meaning: a leaf of a palmtree
KJV renders: branch.

H3713.strongs:
Origin: from 3722;
Meaning: properly, a cover, i.e. (by implication) a tankard (or covered goblet); also white frost (as covering the ground)
KJV renders: bason, hoar(-y) frost.

H3714.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to connect;
