KJV renders: bribe, camphire, pitch, ransom, satisfaction, sum of money, village.

H3725.strongs:
Origin: from 3722;
Meaning: expiation (only in plural)
KJV renders: atonement.

H3726.strongs:
Origin: from 3723 and 5984, with the article interposed; village of the Ammonite;
Meaning: Kefar-ha-Ammoni, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chefarhaamonai.

H3727.strongs:
Origin: from 3722;
Meaning: a lid (used only of the cover of the sacred Ark)
KJV renders: mercy seat.

H3728.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tread down; figuratively, to humiliate
KJV renders: cover.

H3729.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) a root of uncertain correspondence;
Meaning: to fetter
KJV renders: bind.

H3730.strongs:
Origin: or (Amos 9:1) כַּפְתּוֹר; probably from an unused root meaning to encircle;
Meaning: a chaplet; but used only in an architectonic sense, i.e. the capital of a column, or a wreath-like button or disk on the candelabrum
KJV renders: knop, (upper) lintel.

H3731.strongs:
Origin: or (Amos 9:7) כַּפְתּוֹר; apparently the same as 3730;
Meaning: Caphtor (i.e. a wreath-shaped island), the original seat of the Philistines
KJV renders: Caphtor.

H3732.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 3731;
Meaning: a Caphtorite (collectively) or native of Caphtor
KJV renders: Caphthorim, Caphtorim(-s).

H3733.strongs:
