KJV renders: captains, Cherethites (from the margin).

H3747.strongs:
Origin: from 3772; a cut;
Meaning: Kerith, a brook of Palestine
KJV renders: Cherith.

H3748.strongs:
Origin: from 3772;
Meaning: a cutting (of the matrimonial bond), i.e. divorce
KJV renders: divorce(-ment).

H3749.strongs:
Origin: expanded from the same as 3522;
Meaning: a rim or top margin
KJV renders: compass.

H3750.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign origin;
Meaning: the crocus
KJV renders: saffron.

H3751.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Karkemish, a place in Syria
KJV renders: Carchemish.

H3752.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: Karkas, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Carcas.

H3753.strongs:
Origin: from 3769;
Meaning: a dromedary (from its rapid motion as if dancing)
KJV renders: swift beast.

H3754.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Meaning: a garden or vineyard
KJV renders: vines, (increase of the) vineyard(-s), vintage. See also 1021.

H3755.strongs:
Origin: active participle of an imaginary denominative from 3754;
Meaning: a vinedresser
KJV renders: vine dresser (as one or two words).

H3756.strongs:
Origin: from 3754; gardener;
Meaning: Karmi, the name of three Israelites
KJV renders: Carmi.

H3757.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 3756;
Meaning: a Karmite or descendant of Karmi
KJV renders: Carmites.

H3758.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign origin;
Meaning: carmine, a deep red
KJV renders: crimson.

H3759.strongs:
Origin: from 3754;
Meaning: a planted field (garden, orchard, vineyard or park); by implication, garden produce
KJV renders: full (green) ears (of corn), fruitful field (place), plentiful (field).

H3760.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3759;
Meaning: Karmel, the name of a hill and of a town in Palestine
KJV renders: Carmel, fruitful (plentiful) field, (place).

H3761.strongs:
Origin: patron from 3760;
Meaning: a Karmelite or inhabitant of Karmel (the town)
KJV renders: Carmelite.

H3762.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3761;
Meaning: a Karmelitess or female inhabitant of Karmel
KJV renders: Carmelitess.

H3763.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Keran, an aboriginal Idumaean
KJV renders: Cheran.

H3764.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3678;
Meaning: a throne
KJV renders: throne.

H3765.strongs:
Origin: from 3697;
Meaning: to lay waste
KJV renders: waste.

H3766.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to bend the knee; by implication, to sink, to prostrate
KJV renders: bow (down, self), bring down (low), cast down, couch, fall, feeble, kneeling, sink, smite (stoop) down, subdue, × very.

H3767.strongs:
Origin: from 3766;
Meaning: the leg (from the knee to the ankle) of men or locusts (only in the dual)
KJV renders: leg.

H3768.strongs:
Origin: of foreign origin;
Meaning: byssus or fine vegetable wool
KJV renders: green.

H3769.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to dance (i.e. whirl)
KJV renders: dance(-ing).

H3770.strongs:
Origin: by variation from 7164;
Meaning: the paunch or belly (as swelling out)
KJV renders: belly.

H3771.strongs:
Origin: of foreign origin;
Meaning: Karshena, a courtier of Xerxes
KJV renders: Carshena.

H3772.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to cut (off, down or asunder); by implication, to destroy or consume; specifically, to covenant (i.e. make an alliance or bargain, originally by cutting flesh and passing between the pieces)
KJV renders: be chewed, be con-(feder-) ate, covenant, cut (down, off), destroy, fail, feller, be freed, hew (down), make a league (covenant), × lose, perish, × utterly, × want.

H3773.strongs:
Origin: passive participle feminine of 3772;
Meaning: something cut, i.e. a hewn timber
KJV renders: beam.

H3775.strongs:
Origin: apparently by transposition for 3532;
Meaning: a young sheep
KJV renders: lamb.

H3776.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3775;
Meaning: a young ewe
KJV renders: lamb.

H3777.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Meaning: Kesed, a relative of Abraham
KJV renders: Chesed.

H3778.strongs:
Origin: (occasionally with enclitic) כַּשְׂדִּימָה; towards the Kasdites into Chaldea), patronymically from 3777 (only in the plural);
Meaning: a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people
KJV renders: Chaldeans, Chaldees, inhabitants of Chaldea.

H3779.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3778;
Meaning: a Chaldaean or inhabitant of Chaldaea; by implication, a Magian or professional astrologer
KJV renders: Chaldean.

H3780.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to grow fat (i.e. be covered with flesh)
KJV renders: be covered. Compare 3680.

H3781.strongs:
Origin: from 3782;
Meaning: properly, a feller, i.e. an axe
KJV renders: ax.

H3782.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to totter or waver (through weakness of the legs, especially the ankle); by implication, to falter, stumble, faint or fall
KJV renders: bereave (from the margin), cast down, be decayed, (cause to) fail, (cause, make to) fall (down, -ing), feeble, be (the) ruin(-ed, of), (be) overthrown, (cause to) stumble, × utterly, be weak.

H3783.strongs:
Origin: from 3782;
Meaning: properly, a tottering, i.e. ruin
KJV renders: fall.

H3784.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to whisper a spell, i.e. to inchant or practise magic
KJV renders: sorcerer, (use) witch(-craft).

H3785.strongs:
Origin: from 3784;
Meaning: magic
KJV renders: sorcery, witchcraft.

H3786.strongs:
Origin: from 3784;
Meaning: a magician
KJV renders: sorcerer.

H3787.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root properly, to be straight or right;
Meaning: by implication, to be acceptable; also to succeed or prosper
KJV renders: direct, be right, prosper.

H3788.strongs:
Origin: from 3787;
Meaning: success, advantage
KJV renders: equity, good, right.

H3789.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)
KJV renders: describe, record, prescribe, subscribe, write(-ing, -ten).

H3791.strongs:
Origin: from 3789;
Meaning: something written, i.e. a writing, record or book
KJV renders: register, scripture, writing.

H3793.strongs:
Origin: from 3789;
Meaning: a letter or other mark branded on the skin
KJV renders: × any (mark).

H3794.strongs:
Origin: or כִּתִּיִּי; patrial from an unused name denoting Cyprus (only in the plural);
Meaning: a Kittite or Cypriote; hence, an islander in general, i.e. the Greeks or Romans on the shores opposite Palestine
KJV renders: Chittim, Kittim.

H3795.strongs:
Origin: from 3807;
Meaning: beaten, i.e. pure (oil)
KJV renders: beaten.

H3796.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to compact;
Meaning: a wall (as gathering inmates)
KJV renders: wall.

H3798.strongs:
Origin: from 3796 and 376; wall of a man;
Meaning: Kithlish, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Kithlish.

H3799.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to carve or engrave, i.e. (by implication) to inscribe indelibly
KJV renders: mark.
